---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SpeakerPlanner from '../../components/SpeakerPlanner.tsx';

const title = 'Dolby Atmos speaker planner';
const description =
  'Plan Dolby Atmos speakers from 5.1 to 9.1.6: automatic placement in your room, azimuth and elevation angles from the main listening position, checked against Dolby’s installation guidelines.';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'At what angle should Atmos ceiling speakers be mounted?',
    a: 'Dolby’s installation guidelines put top front and top rear speakers at about 45° above horizontal in side view – 30–55° in front, 125–150° measured from the front behind you. With only two ceiling speakers (.2) they sit at about 80°, allowed 65–100°.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where do the surround speakers go?',
    a: 'For 7.1 and 9.1, at the sides at 90–110°, with the rear surrounds at 135–150°. For 5.1 Dolby gives 110–120°, but 90–110° for 5.1.2/5.1.4, so the planner accepts 90–120° for 5.1.x.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How high should the speakers be?',
    a: 'All ear-level speakers at the same height if possible, typically about 1.2 m. Rear speakers may be higher, but no more than 1.25 times the front height. Ceiling speakers at 2 to 3 times the height of the ear-level speakers.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does this cover DTS:X?',
    a: 'The planner checks against Dolby’s guidelines only. We have not evaluated DTS specifications.',
  },
];

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebApplication',
    name: 'Plan My Cinema – Speaker planner',
    url: 'https://plan-my-cinema.com/en/speaker-layout/',
    applicationCategory: 'UtilitiesApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'Web',
    inLanguage: 'en',
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'EUR' },
    description,
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
  },
];
---
<Base lang="en" page="speakers" title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Speaker <span>layout</span></h1>
    <p>Dolby Atmos layouts from 5.1 to 9.1.6 in your room: where each speaker belongs and whether your positions meet Dolby’s angles.</p>
  </div>

  <SpeakerPlanner client:load lang="en" />

  <article class="prose">
    <h2>How the planner works</h2>
    <h3>Based on Dolby’s guidelines</h3>
    <p>
      All angles come from the <a href="https://www.dolby.com/siteassets/technologies/dolby-atmos/atmos-installation-guidelines-121318_r3.1.pdf" rel="noopener">Dolby Atmos Home Theater Installation Guidelines</a>
      (December 2018) and Dolby’s <a href="https://www.dolby.com/about/support/guide/speaker-setup-guides/" rel="noopener">speaker setup guides</a> (March 2020). We did not
      find a newer document.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Channel</th><th>Dolby range</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Left/Right</td><td>22–30° (guidelines fig. 3 says 22–40°)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Centre</td><td>0°</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Wides (9.1.x)</td><td>50–70°</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Surround 7.1/9.1</td><td>90–110°</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Surround 5.1 / 5.1.x</td><td>110–120° / 90–110° (planner: 90–120°)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rear surround</td><td>135–150°</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Top front</td><td>elevation 45° (30–55°)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Top middle (.2 / .6)</td><td>80° (65–100°) / 90° (70–110°)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Top rear</td><td>135° (125–150°)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Dolby’s documents disagree in places: every layout drawing shows 22–30° for left/right, but figure 3 of the guidelines says 22–40°. For 5.1 the
      surrounds sit at 110–120°, for 5.1.2/5.1.4 at 90–110°. The planner shows the narrower range as green and the wider one as yellow.
    </p>

    <h3>Angles</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>Azimuth</strong> is the top-view angle from the main listening position, with 0° pointing at the screen centre. <strong>Elevation</strong> is the
      side-view angle: 0° to the front, 90° straight overhead, 180° to the rear – the same convention Dolby uses.
    </p>

    <h3>Automatic placement</h3>
    <p>
      Unless you enter your own position, the planner puts each speaker at the middle of its Dolby range and moves it out to the wall (15 cm gap).
      Left, centre and right sit behind the screen. Ceiling speakers go on the ceiling, as far out to the side as left/right would be at 30° – which is
      Dolby’s advice for overhead spacing. Use “Move” to enter where a speaker actually is.
    </p>

    <h3>Traffic light</h3>
    <p>
      Green means within Dolby’s range. Yellow means up to 10° outside, or 30–40° for left/right. Red is further out. The 10° margin is our own choice;
      Dolby gives no tolerance beyond its ranges. A yellow speaker usually still works well.
    </p>

    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    {faq.map((f) => (
      <details>
        <summary>{f.q}</summary>
        <p>{f.a}</p>
      </details>
    ))}
  </article>
</Base>
